<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Feb retail sales fall 17.6 pct on year.</title>
<headline>Singapore Feb retail sales fall 17.6 pct on year.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's February retail sales index (base 1991) fell 17.6 percent compared to a year ago, the Department of Statistics said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The figures showed a fall of 30.1 percent from January 1997 sales.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles, the index registered a month-on-month fall of 19.4 percent in February.</p>
<p>February retail sales were estimated at Singapore $1.76 billion. The statistics department said that year-on-year, in constant prices, the retail index fell by 13.7 percent.  </p>
<p>				   Month-on-Month     Yr-on-Yr</p>
<p>    Total index		  -30.1		-17.6</p>
<p>    X-vehicle sales	    -19.4		 -3.3</p>
<p>    Textiles/apparels	  -14.9		  1.8</p>
<p>    Furniture/households     -36.0		  2.2</p>
<p>    Vehicle sales		-65.2		-61.1</p>
<p>    Petrol stations		2.1		 19.0</p>
<p>    Departments/supermarts   -17.3		-13.4</p>
<p>    General provisions	  -8.2		 -5.5</p>
<p>    Other retail		 -23.2		 -4.2</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
